---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = "27 April 2026";
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Interlock Alert"
  description="How Interlock Alert collects, uses and protects personal data — including data captured by alcohol interlock devices and processed through our customer portal."
>
  <section class="hero hero--inner">
    <div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap hero__grid hero__grid--narrow">
      <div class="hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
        <h1 class="display">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="hero__sub">Last updated: {lastUpdated}.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--band">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <article class="legal reveal">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>Interlock Alert Ltd ("Interlock Alert", "we", "our", "us") is a UK company providing pre-drive alcohol screening systems for commercial fleets, businesses and private customers. Our registered address is Interlock Alert, Village Hall, Clifton, Penrith, CA10 2EA. For any privacy-related question, contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@interlockalert.co.uk">privacy@interlockalert.co.uk</a>.</p>
        <p>Interlock Alert is the data controller for the personal data described in this policy, except where we act as a data processor on behalf of a fleet, employer or other organisation that has fitted our devices to vehicles in their control. In those cases, the organisation is the controller and Interlock Alert acts as a processor under their instructions.</p>

        <h2>2. The data we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect the following categories of personal data:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account data</strong> — names, work email addresses, business phone numbers and roles for portal users and primary contacts.</li>
          <li><strong>Test event data</strong> — the result, time, vehicle identifier and GPS location of each breath test, together with a still image or short video clip of the person providing the sample (where the driver-ID camera is enabled).</li>
          <li><strong>Vehicle data</strong> — registration numbers, drivetrain, BAC threshold settings and assignment to drivers or depots.</li>
          <li><strong>Enquiry data</strong> — information you provide when you contact us, request a quote, book a demo, or apply for a pilot programme.</li>
          <li><strong>Site usage data</strong> — limited technical data (IP address, browser, pages visited) collected via essential cookies and standard server logs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. How we use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To deliver the Interlock Alert service — including operating the device on your vehicles, syncing test results to the portal, and sending alerts to your nominated contacts.</li>
          <li>To respond to your enquiries, prepare quotes, and arrange installation appointments.</li>
          <li>To support investigations, audits or compliance reviews initiated by you or your organisation.</li>
          <li>To improve our products, services and documentation, using aggregated and de-identified information where possible.</li>
          <li>To meet our legal, regulatory and contractual obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Lawful bases</h2>
        <p>We rely on the following lawful bases under UK GDPR:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contract</strong> — to deliver the services you have purchased or are evaluating under a pilot.</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — to operate, secure and improve our services, and to send relevant business-to-business communications about pilots, demos and product updates. You can object to processing on this basis at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — to keep records required by tax, accounting and consumer-protection law.</li>
          <li><strong>Consent</strong> — where required, for example for non-essential cookies or for promotional emails to individual subscribers.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Driver identity images and video</h2>
        <p>Where the driver-ID camera is enabled on a vehicle, the device captures a still image — and, depending on configuration, a short video clip — of the person providing the breath sample at the moment of the test. This is to confirm that the test result is attributable to the driver. The images and clips are stored securely on UK-based infrastructure under your account, viewable only by authorised users (such as a fleet manager, line manager or nominated administrator), and retained according to the retention policy your organisation has set.</p>
        <p>If you are a driver and have questions about how this data is being used in your workplace, please raise it directly with your employer, who is the data controller for that data.</p>

        <h2>6. Sharing your data</h2>
        <p>We never sell your data. We share it only with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Sub-processors who help us deliver the service (UK-based hosting, email delivery, customer support tooling). Each is bound by a written data processing agreement.</li>
          <li>Authorised users within your organisation, scoped by role-based access in the portal.</li>
          <li>Law enforcement or regulators where we are legally required to disclose, or where you specifically authorise the release for an investigation.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Where we store data</h2>
        <p>All Interlock Alert customer data is stored on UK-based infrastructure operated by reputable cloud providers. Where international transfer is unavoidable (for example, customer support tools operated by globally distributed vendors), we rely on the UK International Data Transfer Agreement or the EU Standard Contractual Clauses with the UK addendum.</p>

        <h2>8. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>Test event data, including driver-ID images, is retained for the period configured in your customer agreement (typically 12 months by default, configurable per account). Account data is retained for the duration of the contract and a further 6 years to meet UK accounting and tax obligations. Enquiry data submitted via our website is kept for up to 24 months from the last interaction unless we have a continuing relationship with you.</p>

        <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to access, rectify, erase or restrict processing of your personal data, to object to processing, and to data portability. To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:privacy@interlockalert.co.uk">privacy@interlockalert.co.uk</a>. We aim to respond within one calendar month.</p>
        <p>If you are unsatisfied with our response, you have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>

        <h2>10. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>Our website uses only essential cookies required for the site to function, plus a small number of privacy-respecting analytics cookies that help us understand which pages are visited. We do not use third-party advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.</p>

        <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date at the top of this page shows when the most recent change was made. Material changes will be communicated to active customers in advance.</p>

        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:privacy@interlockalert.co.uk">privacy@interlockalert.co.uk</a> or write to: Interlock Alert Ltd, Village Hall, Clifton, Penrith, CA10 2EA.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
